canary PMKCAN-FauJABVy was an argv element of the job and PMK_COMPARE_CANARY held it
in the environment.
mem_canary comes from a page-by-page scan of every readable mapping in
/proc/<pid>/mem.  strings(/proc/<pid>/mem) is not used because it seeks
from offset 0, page 0 is unmapped, the read fails with EIO and it
reports nothing at all, even for the control whose canary sits in its
stack mapping.  The strings_bytes column is that figure, and it is why
the column exists.
